Infer ``None`` for the ``fset`` of a property declared with ``@property`` and no
``.setter``, as CPython does, instead of raising. The lookup escaped as a bare
``StopIteration`` and was reported as a crash on code as simple as ``C.p.fset``.

A property built by a ``property(...)`` call now infers as uninferable rather than
raising, because the setter argument is not modelled and its absence proves nothing.
Property-like decorators that have no ``fset`` at runtime, such as
``functools.cached_property``, keep raising as before.

Closes pylint-dev/pylint#8739
